TestLevels: SDD

Purpose:
  Define test depth levels L0-L5. These levels describe how deep testing
  goes for a given task, not what specific test types to run. The actual
  test types are selected based on level + impact + risk + stack.

Owns: ./

Levels:

  L0:
    name: Smoke
    description: Basic sanity check that the system is up
    scope: critical path only
    speed: very fast (< 30s)
    automation: automated
    applicable_to:
      - deployment verification
      - environment health check
      - post-deployment sanity

  L1:
    name: Unit
    description: Individual components in isolation
    scope: single function/method/component
    speed: fast (< 1s per test)
    automation: automated
    applicable_to:
      - all code changes
      - bug fixes
      - refactoring

  L2:
    name: Integration
    description: Multiple components working together
    scope: component interactions, API contracts, data flow
    speed: medium (1-10s per test)
    automation: automated
    applicable_to:
      - API changes
      - database changes
      - service interactions

  L3:
    name: E2E / UI / Mobile
    description: Full user/business flows
    scope: complete workflows, UI interactions, mobile flows
    speed: slow (10s-5min per test)
    automation: automated + manual
    applicable_to:
      - feature completion
      - UI changes
      - mobile app changes
      - release candidate

  L4:
    name: Performance / Load
    description: System behavior under stress
    scope: load, stress, spike, endurance, scalability
    speed: very slow (minutes to hours)
    automation: automated
    applicable_to:
      - performance-critical systems
      - high-traffic systems
      - before production release

  L5:
    name: Security / Abuse / Disaster
    description: Security validation and disaster recovery
    scope: penetration, abuse, DDoS, disaster recovery
    speed: varies
    automation: automated + manual
    applicable_to:
      - security-critical systems
      - payment systems
      - public-facing systems
      - regulated systems

Selection:
  AI MUST select test level based on:
    Task risk (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL)
    Task impact (isolated/module/project/system)
    Stack (BE/FE/MD/DB/INFRA)
    Security level (L0-L5 from security/levels.sdd)
    Project scale (from PROJECT.sdd)

  Examples:
    LOW risk, isolated impact: L1
    MEDIUM risk, module impact: L1-L2
    HIGH risk, project impact: L1-L3
    CRITICAL risk, system impact: L1-L5

  Test level is NOT the same as SecurityLevel or ProjectLevel.
  These are independent scales.

